module std.witness_admission


data witness_admission_authority_note: String = "Phase 0(b) admission invariant (docs/plans/module-identity-storage-binding-design.md): every enrolled witness row names an executing consumer — discovery rows run per selection; SelfEmitted receipts run on the falsifier wet cadence; known-red quarantined rows run on a probe cadence expecting red (greening is a counted un-quarantine event); operator-ruled OFFLINE rows carry an explicit local-recipe consumer. Enrolled-with-zero-consumers is a typed refusal, never silent. The prior dissolve-on FIRED 2026-07-22: witness exclusion rows now carry derived consumer classification on this module's WitnessConsumerCadence authority (gunbc.ci_layer_roots.witness_exclusion_frontier; group-of-units ruling, gunbc.roster_registry). Homed in dag/std (std.witness_admission) so dag-tree consumers resolve it in dag-only closures — the authority moved here from src/v2/std 2026-07-23 when gunbc.ci_layer_roots became a consumer. This module remains the cadence vocabulary authority; dissolves into the enforcement-intent registry when that thread lands."

type WitnessConsumerCadence
  = DiscoverySelection
  | FalsifierSelfHostWet
  | FalsifierRehomedBinWet
  | FalsifierSubstrateLongLane
  | BinWitnessWet
  | QuarantineProbeExpectRed
  | OfflineLocalRecipe
  | FixtureExplicitRoster
  | NoConsumer

data witness_execution_standing_axis_note: String = "TWO INDEPENDENT AXES, because ALLOWED TO REMAIN and HAS AN EXECUTING CONSUMER are different facts and one success arm cannot carry both (operator ruling on gunbc#7804, 2026-08-04). The first shape of the freeze wall returned WitnessAdmissionHolds — the same arm an executing consumer returns — for a frozen legacy row, and then reported the live gate green as evidence that every current row is admitted. But a frozen row has NO executing consumer; that is the entire content of its debt. Freezing establishes that the unexecuted hole existed at the cut and cannot grow. It does not establish coverage, and returning the success arm made the same fact answer differently depending on which door it entered: exact function-grain admission correctly REFUSES OfflineLocalRecipe because a local recipe is not an executing cadence, while path policy was returning success for exactly that.

AXIS ONE — WitnessExecutionStanding, what actually runs this witness. WitnessHasExecutingConsumer is the only arm that means covered, and it carries WHICH cadence so the claim is checkable rather than a bare yes. LegacyFrozenPathDeferral means the identity is in the frozen baseline: tolerated by the migration ratchet, NOT covered, and anything downstream asking whether the behavior is covered must receive no from this arm. UnclassifiedPathDeferral is a row a broad OfflineLocalRecipe path policy claims but the freeze does not — the forward hole, refused. UnexecutedDeferredWitness is a row nothing claims at all; its remedy is to name a cadence or delete the witness, and it is nearly empty while the path-policy class is in the hundreds, which is why one arm would have hidden the larger population behind the rarer one.

AXIS TWO — FrozenBaselineStanding, whether the migration ratchet still holds, a property of the ROSTER rather than of any row. Allowed and Shrank both permit the tolerated arm; Grew and Stale refuse regardless of any individual row, because a baseline that grew is the escape hatch reopening and a baseline naming a departed witness is an exemption the next witness to take that name inherits.

THE GATES DERIVE, and they are deliberately different: the coverage question admits ONLY WitnessHasExecutingConsumer, so seven hundred dark witnesses never read as covered; the floor gate additionally tolerates LegacyFrozenPathDeferral while axis two holds, so the tree stays green under the ratchet without anything claiming those rows execute."

type WitnessExecutionStanding
  = WitnessHasExecutingConsumer { cadence: WitnessConsumerCadence }
  | LegacyFrozenPathDeferral { entry: String, function: String }
  | UnclassifiedPathDeferral { entry: String, function: String }
  | UnexecutedDeferredWitness { entry: String, function: String }

type FrozenBaselineStanding
  = FrozenBaselineDebtAllowed
  | FrozenBaselineDebtShrank
  | FrozenBaselineDebtGrew { added_count: Int }
  | FrozenBaselineDebtStale { stale_count: Int }

data witness_admission_predicate_dissolution_note: String = "witness_consumer_cadence_is_live / witness_admission_refusal_is_holds dissolved per review 39760 — workflow and tests match the coproducts directly (integration 39758 scaffold superseded on this branch)."

data scheduled_envelope_cadence_wire_note: String = "Temporary wire decoder for ScheduledWitnessEnvelope.cadence (String on the enrollment carrier until that field migrates to WitnessConsumerCadence). THE ONLY home for enrollment wire strings — decode_scheduled_envelope_cadence_wire and compare_declared_derived_enrollment_cadence_wires are the sole round-trip table (five wires: per_pr, 4h, falsifier_substrate_long_lane, offline_local_recipe, no_consumer). Cadences without an enrollment wire (BinWitnessWet, explicit roster, etc.) are carried as WitnessConsumerCadence on admission rows, never as envelope.cadence strings. Dissolve-on: envelope.cadence becomes the closed coproduct and this decoder deletes."

data scheduled_envelope_max_staleness_wire_note: String = "Temporary wire decoder for ScheduledWitnessEnvelope.max_staleness until std.measure lands a typed staleness/deadline carrier. Closed enrollment wires only: 0 (per-PR immediate) and 4h (scheduled tolerance). Anything else is MaxStalenessWireUnrecognized and placement/compare refuse rather than inferring from a bare-string sentinel."

type ScheduledEnvelopeCadenceWireDecode
  = EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: WitnessConsumerCadence }
  | EnvelopeCadenceWireUnrecognized { wire: String }

type ScheduledEnvelopeMaxStalenessWireDecode
  = MaxStalenessPerPrImmediate
  | MaxStalenessScheduledTolerance { wire: String }
  | MaxStalenessWireUnrecognized { wire: String }

type EnrollmentCadenceWireCompare
  = EnrollmentCadenceWiresMatch
  | EnrollmentCadenceWireMismatch {
      declared_cadence: String,
      derived_cadence: String,
    }
  | EnrollmentCadenceWireUnrecognized { wire: String }

fn decode_scheduled_envelope_max_staleness_wire(
  staleness: String,
) -> ScheduledEnvelopeMaxStalenessWireDecode {
  if staleness == "0" {
    MaxStalenessPerPrImmediate
  } else if staleness == "4h" {
    MaxStalenessScheduledTolerance { wire: staleness }
  } else {
    MaxStalenessWireUnrecognized { wire: staleness }
  }
}

fn compare_declared_derived_enrollment_cadence_wires(
  declared_cadence: String,
  derived_cadence: String,
) -> EnrollmentCadenceWireCompare {
  match decode_scheduled_envelope_cadence_wire(cadence: declared_cadence) {
    EnvelopeCadenceWireUnrecognized { wire } =>
      EnrollmentCadenceWireUnrecognized { wire: wire }
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: _ } =>
      if declared_cadence != derived_cadence {
        EnrollmentCadenceWireMismatch {
          declared_cadence: declared_cadence,
          derived_cadence: derived_cadence,
        }
      } else {
        EnrollmentCadenceWiresMatch
      }
  }
}

fn decode_scheduled_envelope_cadence_wire(cadence: String) -> ScheduledEnvelopeCadenceWireDecode {
  if cadence == "per_pr" {
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: DiscoverySelection }
  } else if cadence == "4h" {
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: FalsifierSelfHostWet }
  } else if cadence == "falsifier_substrate_long_lane" {
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: FalsifierSubstrateLongLane }
  } else if cadence == "offline_local_recipe" {
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: OfflineLocalRecipe }
  } else if cadence == "no_consumer" {
    EnvelopeCadenceDecoded { cadence: NoConsumer }
  } else {
    EnvelopeCadenceWireUnrecognized { wire: cadence }
  }
}

fn witness_consumer_cadence_eq(a: WitnessConsumerCadence, b: WitnessConsumerCadence) -> Bool {
  match a {
    DiscoverySelection => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => true
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    FalsifierSelfHostWet => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => true
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    FalsifierRehomedBinWet => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => true
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => true
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    BinWitnessWet => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => true
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    QuarantineProbeExpectRed => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => true
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    OfflineLocalRecipe => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => true
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    FixtureExplicitRoster => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => true
      NoConsumer => false
    }
    NoConsumer => match b {
      DiscoverySelection => false
      FalsifierSelfHostWet => false
      FalsifierRehomedBinWet => false
      FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => false
      BinWitnessWet => false
      QuarantineProbeExpectRed => false
      OfflineLocalRecipe => false
      FixtureExplicitRoster => false
      NoConsumer => true
    }
  }
}

fn witness_consumer_cadence_executes(cadence: WitnessConsumerCadence) -> Bool {
  match cadence {
    QuarantineProbeExpectRed => true
    FalsifierSelfHostWet => true
    FalsifierRehomedBinWet => true
    FalsifierSubstrateLongLane => true
    BinWitnessWet => true
    DiscoverySelection => false
    OfflineLocalRecipe => false
    FixtureExplicitRoster => false
    NoConsumer => false
  }
}
